course: dictionary
lesson: 11407
title: Who is an accountant?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An accountant is a person whose job is to keep and check the money records of a business or a person. They also work out taxes and give advice about money. «My aunt is an accountant, and she checks the money records for her friend's bakery.» The word accountant names a job, so it is a noun.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. Money records, taxes and advice all point to money work. If you put «a teacher» or «a driver» in place of accountant, the sentence stops making sense. That tells you the job is about numbers and money.
explain: In money lessons, accountants track income, which is money coming in, and expenses, which is money going out. They check that the numbers add up. «The accountant noticed the expenses were higher than the income that month.»
fact: An accountant keeps and checks money records.
fact: «Accountant» is a noun, so you can say «an accountant» or «accountants».
fact: «Income» means money coming in, and «expenses» means money going out.
fact: In the UK, a qualified accountant is often called a chartered accountant. In the US, the same kind of qualified accountant is often called a certified public accountant, or CPA.
fact: Families and small businesses often see an accountant at tax time, when they need help with their taxes.
exercise: «My aunt is an accountant, so she checks the money records for her friend's shop.» What is an accountant? | A person who drives a bus | A person who grows vegetables | *A person who keeps and checks money records | A teacher of numbers in a school
exercise: Mum says, «We need to see an accountant before the tax forms are due.» What can an accountant help with? | To learn to swim | To look at the stars | To buy a new bicycle | *Money, taxes and money records
exercise: «The accountant noticed the expenses were higher than the income.» Find and copy the word that means money going out. | income | accountant | noticed | *expenses
test: «Each month the accountant checks that the income and expenses add up.» What must the accountant check? | The shape of the building | *That the money in and money out add up | Who wins the football match | The weather forecast
test: In the US, a qualified accountant is often called a CPA. What does CPA stand for? | Central payment adviser | Careful project administrator | Coins paid annually | *Certified public accountant
exam: «The accountant worked out how much tax the family owed.» What is the accountant's job in this sentence? | To paint the house | *To work out taxes and check the money records | To cook the tea | To drive the family car
